<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tausug</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tausug people, Suluk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tausug are a Muslim people of the Sulu archipelago in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>, with communities also in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">Sabah</a> and other parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mindanao">Mindanao</a>. Their name means people of the current. They formed the core of the Sulu Sultanate, whose society was organised around the sultan and hereditary datus, and they long resisted Spanish and American rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tausug.jpg" alt="Tausug" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jjarivera · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tausug.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
